WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.632
You save a natural language question and

00:00:02.652 --> 00:00:04.010
rerun it next year.

00:00:04.172 --> 00:00:05.647
The words are identical.

00:00:05.796 --> 00:00:07.683
Have you repeated the same search?

00:00:07.871 --> 00:00:09.784
Pause and name what could change between

00:00:09.804 --> 00:00:12.374
your question and the results: generated

00:00:12.394 --> 00:00:15.776
inputs, coverage, indexing, models,

00:00:15.951 --> 00:00:17.605
ranking or control.

00:00:20.002 --> 00:00:22.848
No retrieval method guarantees the same

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.214
records forever.

00:00:24.376 --> 00:00:25.928
The useful question is which parts were

00:00:25.948 --> 00:00:28.892
fixed, documented, exportable and

00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:32.062
versioned. An exact future recreation may

00:00:32.082 --> 00:00:33.854
be impossible, while a saved

00:00:33.874 --> 00:00:36.779
transformation, trace and result export

00:00:36.799 --> 00:00:39.279
still let you compare the later run with

00:00:39.299 --> 00:00:40.206
the original.

00:00:41.108 --> 00:00:43.277
The chapter names four areas.

00:00:43.452 --> 00:00:45.430
Query interpretation records what was

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.110
typed and what was actually sent onward.

00:00:48.285 --> 00:00:51.036
Candidate retrieval records the database,

00:00:51.056 --> 00:00:54.167
fields, indexed unit, retrieval method,

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:56.177
parameters and cutoffs.

00:00:56.326 --> 00:00:58.690
Ranking and fusion records the ordering

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:02.040
stages, component lists and final depth.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:04.614
Retrieval control records whether the

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:08.505
sequence was fixed, adaptive or agentic,

00:01:08.706 --> 00:01:10.567
and the path actually taken.

00:01:10.729 --> 00:01:13.505
Saving only the question leaves all four

00:01:13.525 --> 00:01:15.296
partly unspecified.

00:01:15.458 --> 00:01:18.853
Some details are visible today; internal

00:01:18.873 --> 00:01:21.611
versions and budgets may require vendor

00:01:21.631 --> 00:01:24.137
disclosure. Mark them unknown when

00:01:24.157 --> 00:01:25.077
unavailable.

00:01:26.002 --> 00:01:28.333
Strict Boolean makes inclusion and

00:01:28.353 --> 00:01:29.943
exclusion explicit.

00:01:30.093 --> 00:01:32.302
Eligibility should repeat given the same

00:01:32.322 --> 00:01:35.601
records, indexing, analyser and query

00:01:35.621 --> 00:01:36.670
interpretation.

00:01:36.807 --> 00:01:39.467
Record the exact query, database and

00:01:39.487 --> 00:01:42.908
platform, fields, limits, vocabulary

00:01:42.928 --> 00:01:44.892
version, date and count.

00:01:45.054 --> 00:01:47.276
An unchanged query can still meet a

00:01:47.296 --> 00:01:48.745
changed database.

00:01:49.303 --> 00:01:51.346
Ranked lexical retrieval also needs

00:01:51.366 --> 00:01:54.335
analysis, stemming, field weights,

00:01:54.368 --> 00:01:57.248
rewriting, ranking configuration, sort

00:01:57.268 --> 00:01:58.549
order and depth.

00:01:58.724 --> 00:02:01.720
BM twenty five can move when new records

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.426
change term rarity and document length

00:02:04.446 --> 00:02:07.261
statistics. A stable scoring formula is

00:02:07.281 --> 00:02:09.619
not a frozen collection or a permanent

00:02:09.639 --> 00:02:10.327
ranking.

00:02:11.247 --> 00:02:14.065
A fixed encoder, indexed units, stored

00:02:14.085 --> 00:02:16.797
vectors, similarity function and exact

00:02:16.817 --> 00:02:19.014
search procedure can produce repeatable

00:02:19.034 --> 00:02:22.506
scores. Dense retrieval is not inherently

00:02:22.526 --> 00:02:25.367
random. Record the model and tokeniser

00:02:25.387 --> 00:02:28.137
versions, embedded text and metadata,

00:02:28.299 --> 00:02:31.256
chunking, index version, filters and

00:02:31.276 --> 00:02:33.343
retrieval depth or threshold.

00:02:33.899 --> 00:02:35.940
Ask whether the search was exact or

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.080
approximate. Approximate index

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.283
construction and search parameters can

00:02:40.303 --> 00:02:42.576
affect candidates near a boundary.

00:02:42.726 --> 00:02:44.381
That is a different question from whether

00:02:44.401 --> 00:02:46.830
a language model generated the query

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:49.252
differently. Keep the component and the

00:02:49.272 --> 00:02:51.919
suspected source of variation separate.

00:02:52.827 --> 00:02:54.954
Learnt sparse retrieval can expose

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.968
generated vocabulary terms and weights.

00:02:58.118 --> 00:03:00.366
Those expansions may include terms the

00:03:00.386 --> 00:03:03.085
searcher never typed, so the original

00:03:03.105 --> 00:03:05.481
input alone is insufficient.

00:03:05.657 --> 00:03:08.600
Record the model, tokeniser, index,

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.320
scoring configuration and depth, with

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.497
expansions and weights where available.

00:03:14.045 --> 00:03:16.702
Late interaction can expose query and

00:03:16.722 --> 00:03:18.699
document token alignments.

00:03:18.874 --> 00:03:21.341
It also needs indexed unit boundaries,

00:03:21.361 --> 00:03:24.253
compression and index versions, similarity

00:03:24.273 --> 00:03:26.547
and MaxSim settings, pruning or

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:29.098
approximate search settings and depth.

00:03:29.248 --> 00:03:31.547
Inspectable alignments do not make

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:34.318
contextual vectors portable between model

00:03:34.338 --> 00:03:35.232
versions.

00:03:36.138 --> 00:03:39.528
An LLM rewrite may generate Boolean logic,

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.887
expansion terms, subqueries or

00:03:41.907 --> 00:03:43.278
hypothetical text.

00:03:43.441 --> 00:03:46.088
Save the exact generated form, inferred

00:03:46.108 --> 00:03:49.967
filters, route, prompt or template, parser

00:03:49.987 --> 00:03:52.519
and model versions, and sampling settings

00:03:52.539 --> 00:03:54.142
or seed if exposed.

00:03:54.291 --> 00:03:57.609
Ask whether rerunning reuses that form or

00:03:57.629 --> 00:03:58.768
regenerates it.

00:03:59.327 --> 00:04:01.472
Sampling can introduce deliberate

00:04:01.492 --> 00:04:04.474
variation. Model, prompt and hosted

00:04:04.494 --> 00:04:06.897
inference changes can affect outputs even

00:04:06.917 --> 00:04:08.894
at temperature zero or with greedy

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:11.394
decoding. This does not mean every call

00:04:11.414 --> 00:04:13.997
must vary. Identical output needs a

00:04:14.017 --> 00:04:16.871
guarantee the complete system actually

00:04:16.891 --> 00:04:19.294
provides and tests, rather than an

00:04:19.314 --> 00:04:20.157
assumption.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.766
Fixed and adaptive workflows can document

00:04:23.786 --> 00:04:26.279
rules in advance, but an adaptive branch

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.637
and result dependent query still need a

00:04:28.657 --> 00:04:30.067
record of what happened.

00:04:30.217 --> 00:04:32.697
An agentic sequence can differ between

00:04:32.717 --> 00:04:35.261
runs because it chooses later actions from

00:04:35.281 --> 00:04:36.485
observations.

00:04:37.024 --> 00:04:39.397
Record controller instructions, permitted

00:04:39.417 --> 00:04:42.361
tools and sources, executed queries and

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:45.209
routes, intermediate results, order,

00:04:45.229 --> 00:04:48.443
budgets, stopping and final identifiers.

00:04:48.605 --> 00:04:50.273
What is needed is an action and

00:04:50.293 --> 00:04:53.134
observation trace: what the system did and

00:04:53.154 --> 00:04:54.242
what came back.

00:04:54.391 --> 00:04:56.549
A model’s narrated reasoning is not a

00:04:56.569 --> 00:04:58.327
substitute for that record.

00:04:59.245 --> 00:05:02.671
Keep input, product and mode, search date,

00:05:02.718 --> 00:05:05.791
visible transformations, filters, result

00:05:05.811 --> 00:05:08.407
identifiers, counts and observed

00:05:08.427 --> 00:05:10.971
limitations. Save a raw export where

00:05:10.991 --> 00:05:14.425
possible. Separate direct observation from

00:05:14.445 --> 00:05:17.401
vendor documentation and unknown internal

00:05:17.421 --> 00:05:20.198
details. Ask the institution to obtain

00:05:20.218 --> 00:05:23.523
traces, versions and change notices that

00:05:23.543 --> 00:05:25.687
individuals cannot access.

00:05:26.251 --> 00:05:28.182
The chapter aligns this practice with

00:05:28.202 --> 00:05:30.579
PRISMA S reporting of strategies,

00:05:30.599 --> 00:05:34.058
databases, platforms, limits, dates and

00:05:34.078 --> 00:05:36.636
counts, while recognising replication

00:05:36.656 --> 00:05:39.497
limits. Documentation makes a later

00:05:39.517 --> 00:05:42.254
comparison possible; it does not by itself

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:45.282
explain why a particular paper appeared.

00:05:45.457 --> 00:05:46.996
That is the next film’s question.
